B.aut=new A.pY("Noon Sakinah & Tanween \u2014 Ikhfa","When noon sakinah or tanween is followed by one of 15 letters, hide the noon sound \u2014 ghunnah held two counts, tongue approaching the next letter\u2019s position without touching it.",B.ahp,"Skipping the ghunnah or fully pronouncing the noon is Lahn Jali (major) \u2014 it changes the word. Shortening the ghunnah is Lahn Khafi (minor).","Tuhfat al-Atfal, verses 15\u201318")
B.a3U=s(["\u062a\u064e\u0631\u0652\u0645\u0650\u064a\u0647\u0650\u0645 \u0628\u0650\u062d\u0650\u062c\u064e\u0627\u0631\u064e\u0629\u064d","\u0648\u064e\u0645\u064e\u0627 \u0647\u064f\u0645 \u0628\u0650\u0645\u064f\u0624\u0652\u0645\u0650\u0646\u0650\u064a\u0646\u064e"],t.s)
B.auy=new A.pY("Meem Sakinah \u2014 Ikhfa Shafawi","A meem sakinah followed by \u0628 gets hidden with lip-closure and a two-count ghunnah: not a full meem, not nothing.",B.a3U,"Fully closing to a meem is Lahn Jali; dropping the ghunnah entirely is Lahn Jali; a short ghunnah is Lahn Khafi.","Tuhfat al-Atfal, verse 30")
B.a7n=s(["\u0671\u0644\u0652\u0641\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0642\u0650","\u0648\u064e\u0671\u0644\u0652\u0641\u064e\u062c\u0652\u0631\u0650","\u0639\u064f\u062f\u0652\u0648\u064e\u0627\u0646\u064d\u06e2 \u0641\u0650\u064a\u0647\u0650"],t.s)
B.auv=new A.pY("Qalqalah","The letters \u0642 \u0637 \u0628 \u062c \u062f echo with a slight bounce when sakinah \u2014 strongest when stopping on them, softer mid-word, weakest when carrying them.",B.a7n,"Adding an extra vowel (like a fatha) to the echo is Lahn Jali \u2014 it adds a letter the Quran did not write. A heavy, drawn-out bounce is Lahn Khafi.","Tuhfat al-Atfal, verse 21")
B.a4o=s(["\u0642\u064e\u0627\u0644\u064e","\u064a\u064f\u0648\u0633\u064f\u0641\u064f","\u0641\u0650\u064a\u0647\u0650"],t.s)
B.auu=new A.pY("Madd \u2014 Natural Elongation","A madd letter (\u0627 \u0648 \u064a) with a harakah before it stretches two counts \u2014 the breath\u2019s natural length, never squeezed, never theatrical.",B.a4o,"Cutting a madd to one count is Lahn Khafi in recitation \u2014 makruh, meaning unchanged. Making it comically long is also Lahn Khafi.","Tuhfat al-Atfal, verse 28")
